    "title": "Here’s the prize money payout for each golfer at the LPGA’s 2026 HSBC Women’s World Championship",
    "text": "The LPGA remained in Asia for the second of three events, this being the HSBC Women’s World Championship at Sentosa Golf Club in Singapore. The field of 72 playied for a $3 million purse with the winner taking home $450,000.And that winner was Australian Hannah Green, who captured the event for the second time in three years, topping Auston Kim by a shot after making bogeys on three of the last five holes. This time, however, Green had her husband on the bag to make the victory that much sweeter.Advertisement“I really don’t know what it is but I always enjoy my time in Singapore,” Green said.Green said afterward that she'll now turn her focus to performing better in the major championships, which she did not do last year.Behind Kim there was a three-way tie for third place between Angel Yin, Minjee Lee and Pauline Roussin-Bouchard. World No. 1 Jeeno Thitikul tied for 31st place a week after winning in her native Thailand. It was her worst finish since a missed cut at the U.S. Women's Open last summer.The LPGA now moves to China for the final leg of this Asia swing before taking a week off and returning to the United States.AdvertisementHere’s the rundown of what each player earned this week in Singapore.WIN: Hannah Green, 274/-14, $450,0002: Auston Kim, 275/-13, $279,144T-3: Pauline Roussin-Bouchard, 277/-11, $161,745T-3: Angel Yin, 277/-11, $161,745T-3: Minjee Lee, 277/-11, $161,746: Haeran Ryu, 278/-10, $103,1607: Lindy Duncan, 280/-8, $86,349T-8: Akie Iwai, 281/-7, $71,831T-8: Rio Takeda, 281/-7, $71,831T-10: Charley Hull, 282/-6, $49,478T-10: Esther Henseleit, 282/-6, $49,478T-10: Lottie Woad, 282/-6, $49,478T-10: Miyu Yamashita, 282/-6, $49,478T-10: Mimi Rhodes, 282/-6, $49,478T-10: Julia Lopez Ramirez, 282/-6, $49,478T-10: Andrea Lee, 282/-6, $49,478AdvertisementT-10: Linn Grant, 282/-6, $49,478T-18: Cassie Porter, 283/-5, $36,475T-18: Youmin Hwang, 283/-5, $36,475T-18: Ariya Jutanugarn, 283/-5, $36,475T-21: Chizzy Iwai, 284/-4, $30,949T-21: Mao Saigo, 284/-4, $30,949T-21: Hye-Jin Choi, 284/-4, $30,949T-21: Hyo Joo Kim, 284/-4, $30,949T-21: Sei Young Kim, 284/-4, $30,949T-21: Ayaka Furue, 284/-4, $30,94T-27: Gaby Lopez, 285/-3, $25,484T-27: Lydia Ko, 285/-3, $25,484T-27: Yan Liu, 285/-3, $25,484T-27: Allisen Corpuz, 285/-3, $25,484T-31: Minami Katsu, 286/-2, $22,160T-31: Jeeno Thitikul, 286/-2, $22,160T-31: Nanna Koerstz Madsen, 286/-2, $22,160T-34: Yujie Liu, 287/-1, $0 (amateur)AdvertisementT-34: Jenny Shin, 287/-1, $18,416T-34: Gurleen Kaur, 287/-1, $18,416T-34: Brooke Matthews 287/-1, $18,416T-34: Wei-Ling Hsu, 287/-1, $18,416T-34: Brooke Henderson, 287/-1, $18,416T-34: Saki Baba, 287/-1, $18,416T-41: Grace Kim, 288/E, $14,391T-41: Chanettee Wannasaen, 288/E, $14,391T-41: Carlota Ciganda, 288/E, $14,391T-41: Ina Yoon, 288/E, $14,391T-41: Ruoning Yin, 288/E, $14,391T-41: Leona Maguire, 288/E, $14,391T-47: Jin Young Ko, 289/+1, $11,614T-47: Megan Khang, 289/+1, $11,614T-47: Yuri Yoshida, 289/+1, $11,614T-47: Gemma Dryburgh, 289/+1, $11,614T-47: Karis Anne Davidson, 289/+1, $11,614AdvertisementT-52: A Lim Kim, 290/+2, $10,087T-52: Celine Boutier, 290/+2, $10,087T-52: Nataliya Guseva, 290/+2, $10,087T-55: Lucy Li, 291/+3, $9,323T-55: Manon De Roey, 291/+3, $9,32357: Jin Hee Im, 292/+4, $8,863T-58: Mi Hyang Lee, 293/+5, $8,406T-58: Pajaree Anannarukarn, 293/+5, $8,406T-60: Xingtong Chen, 294/+6, $0 (amateur)T-60: Benedetta Moresco, 294/+6, $7,604T-60: Robyn Choi, 294/+6, $7,604T-60: Jenny Bae, 294/+6, $7,604T-60: Jennifer Kupcho, 294/+6, $7,604T-65: Yealimi Noh, 295/+7, $7,107T-65: Somi Lee, 295/+7, $7,107T-67: Yuka Saso, 296/+8, $6,800T-67: Lilia Vu, 296/+8, $6,80069: Shannon Tan, 297/+9, $6,57370: Paula Reto, 300/+12, $6,41871: Stephanie Kyriacou, 311/+23, $6,26672: Ingrid Lindblad, 312/+24, $6,114",
